    "q-152917": {
      "dom_id": "step-q152917",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2x},\\,1\\le x\\le {e}^{2}.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fourth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{4}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\,{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}({e}^{8}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{8}-1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
